{"author":{"id":"0fb62b7075a4219f84b4bf8c9c235af1632f3fa4b63ca899f025ad8215a930fd"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778070873,"nonce":"am9S7/6f2l31XII5jZFlCOVsuZI=","title":"validate_masters() in R/utils.R returns a tibble of warnings/errors but never raises. data-raw/masters.R calls it after each institution and after the merge, then proceeds to write data/masters.RDS regardless of the result. A schema-level regression today would still produce an output file.","message":"This is the kind of guard that would have caught the Oslomet GFU_2024 omission earlier if it included a row-count or value-domain check.\n\n- Have validate_masters() return invisibly when clean and `stop()` (or `rlang::abort`) when any row has `warning == \"error\"`. Keep `warning == \"warning\"` as a message.\n- Update data-raw/masters.R so validation failure halts the pipeline before write_rds().\n- Decide if extra columns (\"warning\") should also fail in CI but pass interactively.\n\nCurrently expected_cols covers id, institution_short, collection, GLU, year, authors, n_authors, url, language, full_text_available, subject, title, abstract, title_alt, abstract_alt with their types. The extra-column case is currently a \"warning\" — keep that level.\n\nIndependent of the Oslomet bug but a prerequisite for adding value-level tests (separate bug) — both should share the same error-raising mechanism.","files":null}]}